      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5f2eb932b923f7086bb2aed2",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Build 976 have improved the behaviour, but it's still buggy and not like before. For AV2 and AV3 Avatars:\nPress the trigger down will now result to smooth analog values between 0 and 1 (perfect!). But releasing the trigger lower than 90% of the pressed value, will let it fall immediately to 0 (visible too in debug window). So, an analog position is only possible for pressing, not for releasing the trigger.\nExpected behaviour:\nGestureRightWeight/GestureLeftWeight should always match the current value of the physical position of the trigger.\nAlso I have remarked a second issue on this:\nI have updated my finger point animation for my avatar 3.0. First keyframe is idle position. Second position is the finger point position. Pressing the trigger down from 0 to 0.99 will smoothly move between this two keyframes. But on value 1, the animation falls back to idle position of the first keyframe. \nThis has also this bad sideeffect:\nWhen i dont use the trigger and only use the touch pad (where GestureRightWeight/GestureLeftWeight is always 1), the animation doesnt work.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
